  "stem": "A line in the \\(xy\\)-plane passes through the points \\((2, 1)\\) and \\((6, 11)\\). The line crosses the \\(y\\)-axis at the point \\((0, b)\\). What is the value of \\(b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "-4"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Slope \\(= \\frac{11 - 1}{6 - 2} = \\frac{5}{2}\\).",
    "Use \\((2, 1)\\): \\(1 = \\frac{5}{2}(2) + b = 5 + b\\), so \\(b = -4\\)."
  ],
  "verify": "m = Rational(11 - 1, 6 - 2)\nb = 1 - m*2\nassert b == -4 and 11 - m*6 == b\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [b]",
